hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1638","**\nNarrated to us Abu Hashim Ziyad ibn Ayyub and Ahmad ibn Mani’: They said, narrated to us Hushaym, who informed us Ya’la ibn ‘Ata’.\n\nAnd it was also narrated to us Bundar, who said, narrated to us Muhammad.\n\nAnd it was also narrated to us al-San’ani, who narrated to us Khalid, who said, narrated to us Shu’ba.\n\nAnd narrated to us Ahmad ibn Mani’, who narrated to us Yazid ibn Harun, who informed us Hisham ibn Hassan, Shu’ba, and Sharik.\n\nAnd narrated to us Salam ibn Junada, who narrated to us Waki’, from Sufyan—all of them from Ya’la ibn ‘Ata’, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father.\n\nHushaym said: “This is his hadith.” He said: narrated to us Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad al-‘Amiri, from his father, who said:\n\n“I witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) his Farewell Pilgrimage. He said: So I prayed the Fajr prayer with him in the Mosque of al-Khayf, meaning the Mosque of Mina. When he completed his prayer, he noticed two men at the end of the congregation who had not prayed with him. He said: ‘Bring them to me.’ So they were brought to him, their limbs trembling. He said: ‘What prevented you from praying with us?’ They said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in our places.’ He said: ‘Do not do that. If you pray in your places, then come to a congregational mosque and pray with them, for it will be a voluntary prayer for you.’”\n\nBundar said: “So you came to the imam while he had not yet prayed.”\n\nIn the narration of Waki’: “Then you came while the people were in the prayer.”\n\nAl-San’ani added: “And the people were taking his hand and wiping their faces with it. It was cooler than snow and more fragrant than musk.”"
